  <main_text>
    <l n="1">9. Donatio ex causis ingratitudinis revo-</l>
    <l n="2">cari potest.</l>
    <l n="3">10. Etiam pro parte, si facta sit liberis ex-</l>
    <l n="4">tantibus.</l>
    <l n="5">11. Non tamen ob supervenientiam libe-</l>
    <l n="6">rorum revocabitur.</l>
    <l n="7">12. Moribus forte secus, &amp; jure Canonico.</l>
    <l n="8" type="heading" level="3" para="true">§. 3.</l>
    <l n="9">1. Explicatur propter nuptias donatio.</l>
    <l n="10">2. Comparantur dos &amp; donatio propter</l>
    <l n="11">nuptias.</l>
    <l n="12">3. Non tamen per omnia.</l>
    <l n="13">4. Utilitas donationis propter nuptias as-</l>
    <l n="14">signatur.</l>
    <l n="15">5. Non ea confundenda cum sponsalitiâ</l>
    <l n="16">largitate.</l>
    <l n="17">6. Mores allegantur.</l>
    <l n="18" type="heading" level="3" para="true">§. 4.</l>
    <l n="19">1. Singularis adquirendi modus per jus</l>
    <l n="20">adcrescendi.</l>
    <l n="21">2. Quid jure Hebraeorum obtineat?</l>
    <l n="22" type="heading" level="1" caput="2" para="true">LIBR. 2. TIT. 8.</l>
    <l n="23" type="heading" level="2" para="true">Quibus alienare licet, vel non.</l>
    <l n="24" type="heading" level="3" para="true">In Princ.</l>
    <l n="25" para="true">1. Dominus regulariter rem suam</l>
    <l n="26">alienare non prohibetur.</l>
    <l n="27">2. Exceptio proponitur in marito dotis no-</l>
    <l n="28">mine.</l>
    <l n="29">3. Idem in sponso admittendum.</l>
    <l n="30">4. Non idem forte si pecuniâ dotali praedi-</l>
    <l n="31">um sit comparatum.</l>
    <l n="32">5. Prohibitio etiam ad rem mobilem ex-</l>
    <l n="33">tenditur.</l>
    <l n="34">6. Alienationis nomine quid veniat?</l>
    <l n="35">7. Mores describuntur.</l>
    <l n="36">8. Jus Canonicum allegatur.</l>
    <l n="37" type="heading" level="2" para="true">§. 1.</l>
    <l n="38" para="true">1. Creditor, licet non sit Dominus, pignus</l>
    <l n="39">alienare potest.</l>
    <l n="40" para="true">2. Species pignorum &amp; distrahendi modi</l>
    <l n="41">proponuntur.</l>
    <l n="42" para="true">3. Mores allegantur.</l>
    <l n="43" type="heading" level="2" para="true">§. 2.</l>
    <l n="44" para="true">1. Pupillus sine tutore non recte alienat.</l>
    <l n="45" para="true">2. Ea propter non potest pecuniam mutuam</l>
    <l n="46">dare.</l>
    <l n="47" para="true">3. Repeti, vel condici pecunia potest.</l>
    <l n="48" para="true">4. Pupillo tamen mutuo dari potest.</l>
    <l n="49" para="true">5. Non recte solvitur pupillo.</l>
    <l n="50" para="true">6. Moribus quid desideretur?</l>
    <l n="51" para="true">7. Non denique quod debet solvere potest</l>
    <l n="52">pupillus.</l>
    <l n="53" type="heading" level="1" para="true">Libr. 2. Instit. Tit. 9.</l>
    <l n="54" type="heading" level="2" para="true">Per quas personas cuique adquiritur.</l>
    <l n="55" type="heading" level="2" para="true">In Princ.</l>
    <l n="56" para="true">1. Quaedam adquiruntur civiliter,</l>
    <l n="57">quaedam naturaliter.</l>
    <l n="58" para="true">2. In imperio Monasterio per Monachos</l>
    <l n="59">non adquiritur.</l>
    <l n="60" type="heading" level="2" para="true">§. 1.</l>
    <l n="61" para="true">1. Jure antiquo quid per liberos adquira-</l>
    <l n="62">tur?</l>
    <l n="63" para="true">2. Quid jure novo, &amp; novissimo?</l>
    <l n="64" para="true">3. Quanam peculio profectitio adnume-</l>
    <l n="65">rentur?</l>
    <l n="66" para="true">4. Quid statuendum de muneribus quae</l>
    <l n="67">dantur filiolis à fonte baptismatis su-</l>
    <l n="68">blatis?</l>
    <l n="69" para="true">5. Quis usus peculiis profectitiis?</l>
    <l n="70" para="true">6. Moribus à jure civilis recessum est.</l>
    <l n="71" type="heading" level="2" para="true">§. 2.</l>
    <l n="72" para="true">Jus anterius circa peculium aliquam</l>
    <l n="73">continebat iniquitatem.</l>
    <l n="74" type="heading" level="2" para="true">§. 3.</l>
  </main_text>
  <notes>Right edge of the page is cut off; the ends of some lines are missing and are not reproduced. Some numerals and letters in the first lines are uncertain.</notes>
